## Anti Patterns (Các pattern cần tránh)

### 1. Entities with Dependencies
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Entity depends on infrastructure
class Order {
  constructor(private db: Database) {} // Wrong!
}

// ✅ GOOD: Pure entity
class Order {
  // No dependencies
}
```

### 2. Use Cases with Framework Code
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Use case has HTTP concerns
class CreateOrderUseCase {
  async execute(req: Request, res: Response) {
    res.json({ orderId: order.id });
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Use case is framework-agnostic
class CreateOrderUseCase {
  async execute(input: CreateOrderInput): Promise<CreateOrderOutput> {
    // Pure business logic
  }
}
```

### 3. Dependencies Pointing Outward
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Domain imports infrastructure
import { PostgresOrderRepository } from 'infrastructure';

class OrderService {
  private repo: PostgresOrderRepository; // Wrong!
}

// ✅ GOOD: Depend on abstractions
class OrderService {
  private repo: IOrderRepository; // Right!
}
```

## Best Practices (Thực hành tốt nhất)

1. **Dependencies point inward**: Outer layers depend on inner layers
2. **Entities are pure**: No dependencies on frameworks or external services
3. **Use cases orchestrate**: Don't put business logic in controllers
4. **Define interfaces in use case layer**: Infrastructure implements them
5. **Composition root**: Wire dependencies in one place
6. **Frameworks are plugins**: Can be swapped without changing core
7. **Test business rules first**: Domain should be highly testable
8. **Keep use cases focused**: Single responsibility
9. **Preserve encapsulation**: Don't expose entities directly
10. **Document architecture decisions**: ADRs for major choices

